  "question": {
    "text": "A nucleus of mass $M+\\Delta m$ is at rest and decays into two daughter nuclei of equal mass $\\frac{M}{2}$ each. Speed of light is $\\mathrm{C}$.\nThe speed of daughter nuclei is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$c \\frac{\\Delta m}{M+\\Delta m}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$c \\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\Delta m}{M}}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$c \\sqrt{\\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{m}}{\\mathrm{M}}}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$c \\sqrt{\\frac{\\Delta m}{M+\\Delta m}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Conserving the momentum\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\n0=\\frac{\\mathrm{M}}{2} \\mathrm{~V}_1-\\frac{\\mathrm{M}}{2} \\mathrm{~V}_2 \\\\\n\\mathrm{~V}_1=\\mathrm{V}_2 \\quad \\quad \\ldots \\ldots (1) \\\\\n\\Delta \\mathrm{mc}^2=\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{M}}{2} \\mathrm{~V}_1^2+\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{M}}{2} \\cdot \\mathrm{V}_2^2 \\quad \\quad \\ldots \\ldots (2)\\\\\n\\Delta \\mathrm{mc}^2=\\frac{\\mathrm{M}}{2} \\mathrm{~V}_1^2 \\\\\n\\frac{2 \\Delta \\mathrm{mc}^2}{\\mathrm{M}}=\\mathrm{V}_1^2 \\\\\n\\mathrm{~V}_1=\\mathrm{c} \\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\Delta \\mathrm{m}}{\\mathrm{M}}}\n\\end{gathered}\n$$"
  }
